--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Analytics/**`. That path
is NOT a project.yml source group in this repo. The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — every sibling analytics page (FleetCompare, Statistics,
Mileage, LifetimeStats, TrueCost) and the done `page:admin/ApiPlayground` live there; `Sources` IS a
project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/**` (+ tests at `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/**`)
— the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Analytics`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). Navigation registration touches the
allowed `Sources/App/AppRoute.swift` + `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`. This mapping is the only deviation
from the literal prompt path.

ONE FORCED RENAME (no silent drift): the page's display-boundary formatter was authored as
`WeeklyDigestFormat`, which COLLIDES with a pre-existing module-level `enum WeeklyDigestFormat` in
`TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/WeeklyDigestWidget.Adapter.swift` (same app module → redeclaration). It was
renamed to `WeeklyDigestPageFormat` (file `WeeklyDigestPageFormat.swift`) to keep the app target
compiling. All 40+ of my other `WeeklyDigest*` type names were verified unique against the existing
widget types (only `…Format` clashed).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE NOTE (no scope narrowing — covenant #2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The manifest extracted this page as "no panels / no charts / renders from local state" (its 8 required
items are the 3 data states + 5 page-level strings), because WeeklyDigestPage.tsx delegates its body to
imported section components (WeekSelector, SummaryHeroCards, DrivingSection, ChargingSection,
BatteryHealthSection, AlertsSection, WeekOverWeekSummary) rather than inline <GlassPanel>s. Per covenant
#2/#5 + the Acceptance Criteria ("reproduce every region from the web source"), ALL seven sections were
implemented natively (not just the 8 gate items), including the two daily bar charts (Swift Charts) and
the alert-distribution pie. The deterministic digest aggregation (web `useWeeklyDigest` hook) was ported
verbatim into a pure, unit-tested `WeeklyDigestEngine`.

UNITS NOTE (ADR-005): the web page applies NO per-user unit preference (it renders literal km / kWh / kW
/ Wh/km, only routing currency through `formatCurrency`). For faithful semantic parity the native page
does the same: models store SI canonical (meters / watt-hours / seconds / watts), and `WeeklyDigestPageFormat`
converts at the render boundary (m→km, Wh→kWh, W→kW). No KMP `Units`/`Shared` dependency is pulled into
this page (matching the web's literal-unit behaviour), which also keeps it isolated-typecheck-verifiable.

